9. Gaussian matrices against the ceiling for a round cloud
   No region of a code in 8 dimensions does better on a round cloud than a ball, and no cell than a ball's (the plan gives the proof).
   floor = G of the ball in 8 dimensions * region part of the ball for Gaussian blocks, from its integral * codewords^(-1/4).
